From e0a31d495fefcea597d35308456d1767863ff4fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Salveti <ricardo.salveti@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 01:09:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] deploy: add sealed UKI support

Support booting an ostree deployment from a Unified Kernel Image whose
kernel command line is embedded (and typically signed for UEFI Secure
Boot) in its .cmdline PE section, and publishing those UKIs as Boot
Loader Specification type-2 entries.

A sealed UKI cannot carry the mutable ostree=/ostree/boot.BOOTVERSION/...
bootlink argument (bootversion and bootserial are assigned at deploy
time), so it embeds a fixed selector argument instead:

    ostree=/ostree/root.BOOTID

where BOOTID is chosen when the UKI is built and shipped in the
deployment tree as usr/lib/modules/KVER/ostree-boot-id next to uki.efi.
ostree-prepare-root already resolves any symlink target of the ostree=
argument, so no boot-side change is needed.

At deploy time, for a UKI deployment that ships an ostree-boot-id:

- maintain the /ostree/root.BOOTID symlink pointing at the deployment
  directory (same shape as the aboot slot links);
- write the loader entry without an options line so systemd-boot passes
  no load options and systemd-stub uses the embedded command line
  regardless of Secure Boot state; record the bootlink in an
  x-ostree-bootlink vendor key so deployments stay enumerable;
- garbage-collect dangling /ostree/root.* selector symlinks.

The system generator resolves the stateroot through the selector symlink
(like aboot), the soft-reboot karg comparison tolerates deployments
without bootconfig kargs, and ostree_bootconfig_parser_set() learns to
remove a key when passed NULL.

When sysroot.sd-boot-type2 is additionally set, the sealed UKIs are
published into EFI/Linux/ostree-INDEX-BOOTID[+TRIES].efi so systemd-boot
auto-discovers them as type-2 entries ordered by file name; no type-1
entries are written for the boot loader to read, and ostree keeps its
bookkeeping fragments in loader/entries.ostree (which the boot loader
does not scan) with a read-path fallback to the classic entries
directory for pre-migration deployments. The UKIs are published from the
systemd-boot backend: write_config builds and validates a publish plan
before the boot-directory swap (so errors leave the running system
untouched) and post_bls_sync executes it afterwards, installing fresh
UKIs and renaming existing ones for index changes while preserving the
live boot-counter suffix. Stale and orphaned EFI/Linux UKIs are reaped
in the boot filesystem cleanup, and loader.conf gets a "default ostree-*"
line so a stray higher-sorting .efi cannot become the default.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Ricardo Salveti <ricardo.salveti@oss.qualcomm.com>
